  <text>
    <body>
      <p>George Yelland, hair cutter and later hairdresser, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref> in every Sands &amp; McDougall directory from 1857 to 1868 except 1863 and 1864.</p>
      <p>His number changes as the street is numbered: no number in 1857 and 1858, No. 9 in 1859, No. 11 in 1860 and 1861, and No. 17 from 1862 to 1868. From 1865 he is listed as "Yelland, G." without a trade.</p>
      <p>A "Yelland, G." is listed at 64 Bouverie Street in 1863, and a Wm. G. Yelland at 1 Lincoln Cottages in 1910. It isn't clear they are the same person.</p>
    </body>
